@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1792 = private unnamed_addr constant [642 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for \22HACK\22 comments.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A\22HACK\22 comments are used to describe an issue that should be resolved\0A(usually, a suboptimal solution or temporary workaround).\0A\0AConsider resolving the issue before deploying the code.\0A\0ANote that if you use \22HACK\22 comments as a form of documentation, this\0Arule may not be appropriate for your project.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport os\0A\0A\0Adef running_windows():  # HACK: Use platform module instead.\0A    try:\0A        os.mkdir(\22C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\\22)\0A    except FileExistsError:\0A        return True\0A    else:\0A        os.rmdir(\22C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\\22)\0A        return False\0A```\0A", align 1
