@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1800 = private unnamed_addr constant [513 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for unnecessary dictionary unpacking operators (`**`).\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AUnpacking a dictionary into another dictionary is redundant. The unpacking\0Aoperator can be removed, making the code more readable.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afoo = {\22A\22: 1, \22B\22: 2}\0Abar = {**foo, **{\22C\22: 3}}\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afoo = {\22A\22: 1, \22B\22: 2}\0Abar = {**foo, \22C\22: 3}\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: Dictionary displays](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/expressions.html#dictionary-displays)\0A", align 1
