@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1830 = private unnamed_addr constant [655 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for Python version comparisons that compare against a tuple of the\0Awrong length.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AStub files support simple conditionals to test for differences in Python\0Aversions and platforms. When comparing against `sys.version_info`, avoid\0Acomparing against tuples of the wrong length, which can lead to unexpected\0Abehavior.\0A\0A## Example\0A```pyi\0Aimport sys\0A\0Aif sys.version_info[:2] == (3,): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```pyi\0Aimport sys\0A\0Aif sys.version_info[0] == 3: ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Typing documentation: Version and Platform checking](https://typing.python.org/en/latest/spec/directives.html#version-and-platform-checks)\0A", align 1
