@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1842 = private unnamed_addr constant [617 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the presence of unused private `TypeVar`, `ParamSpec` or\0A`TypeVarTuple` declarations.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AA private `TypeVar` that is defined but not used is likely a mistake. It\0Ashould either be used, made public, or removed to avoid confusion. A type\0Avariable is considered \22private\22 if its name starts with an underscore.\0A\0A## Example\0A```pyi\0Aimport typing\0Aimport typing_extensions\0A\0A_T = typing.TypeVar(\22_T\22)\0A_Ts = typing_extensions.TypeVarTuple(\22_Ts\22)\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThe fix is always marked as unsafe, as it would break your code if the type\0Avariable is imported by another module.\0A", align 1
