@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1874 = private unnamed_addr constant [545 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for strings that include unnecessarily escaped quotes.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIf a string contains an escaped quote that doesn't match the quote\0Acharacter used for the string, it's unnecessary and can be removed.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afoo = \22bar\\'s\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afoo = \22bar's\22\0A```\0A\0A## Formatter compatibility\0AWe recommend against using this rule alongside the [formatter]. The\0Aformatter automatically removes unnecessary escapes, making the rule\0Aredundant.\0A\0A[formatter]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/formatter\0A", align 1
