@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1918 = private unnamed_addr constant [1037 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for missing blank lines between top level functions and classes.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APEP 8 recommends exactly two blank lines between top level functions and classes.\0A\0AThe rule respects the [`lint.isort.lines-after-imports`] setting when\0Adetermining the required number of blank lines between top-level `import`\0Astatements and function or class definitions for compatibility with isort.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef func1():\0A    pass\0Adef func2():\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef func1():\0A    pass\0A\0A\0Adef func2():\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0A## Typing stub files (`.pyi`)\0AThe typing style guide recommends to not use blank lines between classes and functions except to group\0Athem. That's why this rule is not enabled in typing stub files.\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.isort.lines-after-imports`\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 8: Blank Lines](https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#blank-lines)\0A- [Flake 8 rule](https://www.flake8rules.com/rules/E302.html)\0A- [Typing Style Guide](https://typing.python.org/en/latest/source/stubs.html#blank-lines)\0A", align 1
