@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1941 = private unnamed_addr constant [2236 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for lines that exceed the specified maximum character length.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AOverlong lines can hurt readability. [PEP 8], for example, recommends\0Alimiting lines to 79 characters. By default, this rule enforces a limit\0Aof 88 characters for compatibility with Black and the Ruff formatter,\0Athough that limit is configurable via the [`line-length`] setting.\0A\0AIn the interest of pragmatism, this rule makes a few exceptions when\0Adetermining whether a line is overlong. Namely, it:\0A\0A1. Ignores lines that consist of a single \22word\22 (i.e., without any\0A   whitespace between its characters).\0A2. Ignores lines that end with a URL, as long as the URL starts before\0A   the line-length threshold.\0A3. Ignores line that end with a pragma comment (e.g., `# type: ignore`\0A   or `# noqa`), as long as the pragma comment starts before the\0A   line-length threshold. That is, a line will not be flagged as\0A   overlong if a pragma comment _causes_ it to exceed the line length.\0A   (This behavior aligns with that of the Ruff formatter.)\0A4. Ignores SPDX license identifiers and copyright notices\0A   (e.g., `# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`), which are machine-readable\0A   and should _not_ wrap over multiple lines.\0A\0AIf [`lint.pycodestyle.ignore-overlong-task-comments`] is `true`, this rule will\0Aalso ignore comments that start with any of the specified [`lint.task-tags`]\0A(e.g., `# TODO:`).\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Amy_function(param1, param2, param3, param4, param5, param6, param7, param8, param9, param10)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Amy_function(\0A    param1, param2, param3, param4, param5,\0A    param6, param7, param8, param9, param10\0A)\0A```\0A\0A## Error suppression\0AHint: when suppressing `E501` errors within multi-line strings (like\0Adocstrings), the `noqa` directive should come at the end of the string\0A(after the closing triple quote), and will apply to the entire string, like\0Aso:\0A\0A```python\0A\22\22\22Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet.\0A\0ALorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit, sed do eiusmod tempor.\0A\22\22\22  # noqa: E501\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `line-length`\0A- `lint.task-tags`\0A- `lint.pycodestyle.ignore-overlong-task-comments`\0A- `lint.pycodestyle.max-line-length`\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#maximum-line-length\0A", align 1
