@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1968 = private unnamed_addr constant [1077 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for class methods that are not separated from the class's docstring\0Aby a blank line.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A[PEP 257] recommends the use of a blank line to separate a class's\0Adocstring from its methods.\0A\0AThis rule may not apply to all projects; its applicability is a matter of\0Aconvention. By default, this rule is enabled when using the `numpy` and `pep257`\0Aconventions, and disabled when using the `google` convention.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aclass PhotoMetadata:\0A    \22\22\22Metadata about a photo.\22\22\22\0A    def __init__(self, file: Path):\0A        ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aclass PhotoMetadata:\0A    \22\22\22Metadata about a photo.\22\22\22\0A\0A    def __init__(self, file: Path):\0A        ...\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.pydocstyle.convention`\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 257 \E2\80\93 Docstring Conventions](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/)\0A- [NumPy Style Guide](https://numpydoc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/format.html)\0A- [Google Python Style Guide - Docstrings](https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#38-comments-and-docstrings)\0A\0A[PEP 257]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/\0A", align 1
